msgid "the mount on which to take a write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/api-summary:101: ../fs/namespace.c:462
msgid ""
"This tells the low-level filesystem that a write is about to be performed to "
"it, and makes sure that writes are allowed (mnt it read-write) before "
"returning success. This operation does not protect against filesystem being "
"frozen. When the write operation is finished, mnt_put_write_access() must be "
"called. This is effectively a refcount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/api-summary:101: ../fs/namespace.c:519
msgid "get write access to a mount"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/api-summary:101: ../fs/namespace.c:521
msgid ""
"This tells the low-level filesystem that a write is about to be performed to "
"it, and makes sure that writes are allowed (mount is read-write, filesystem "
"is not frozen) before returning success.  When the write operation is "
"finished, mnt_drop_write() must be called.  This is effectively a refcount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/api-summary:101: ../fs/namespace.c:563
msgid "get write access to a file's mount"
